# {{ name | default('trajectory-monitor') }}

Compares current stage output against a baseline (SPEC → PLAN → original prompt,
multi-layer fallback) and returns a drift score in [0.0, 1.0]. A score > the
configured threshold (`harness.yaml.drift.threshold`, default 0.7) signals
trajectory drift and surfaces in the stage's review report.

Implements ADR-010 hybrid drift score: cosine similarity is computed first;
only when `cos_sim < threshold` does the LLM precision judge run, keeping
LLM cost low while preserving precision on suspicious cases.


## When to invoke

- After `execute` finishes implementing a phase — verify the diff still
  serves the SPEC's acceptance criteria, not a hallucinated alternative.
- During `review` consensus when the surface findings disagree on whether
  the implementation matches intent.
- On `wrapup` immediately before commit — last-line defense against
  silent scope creep.


## When to skip

- Stage output empty or `< 100` chars (no signal to compare).
- No baseline available (no SPEC, no PLAN, no captured user prompt) — the
  monitor would have nothing to anchor against.
- `harness.yaml.drift.disabled: true` (user explicit opt-out).


## How it runs

```bash
uv run --with {{ harness_maker_src_path }} python -m harness_maker.drift_monitor \
    --baseline-spec specs/SPEC-{{ '{slug}' }}.md \
    --baseline-plan work-docs/plans/PLAN-{{ '{slug}' }}.md \
    --baseline-prompt "<original-user-request>" \
    --current-text "<current-stage-output>"
```

The CLI prints a JSON object: `{"drift_score": 0.42, "method": "cosine|llm",
"baseline_source": "spec|plan|prompt", "verdict": "on-track|drift"}`.


## Outputs

- Drift score, method (cosine fast path vs. LLM precision), baseline source.
- Verdict (`on-track` or `drift`). Verdict `drift` should attach to the
  stage report under "Drift Findings" — ⚠️ severity, link the diverging
  passage, suggest re-aligning to the SPEC item.

The skill is read-only. Acting on a drift verdict is the orchestrating
stage's responsibility, not this skill's.
